      "id": 1,
      "text": "Industrialisation turned Docklands’ swamp land into a bustling dock area in the 1880s, reshaping the waterfront.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.victoriaharbour.com.au/discover/history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Docklands takes its name from Batman’s Hill, a historic landmark that once stood within the precinct.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Docklands%2C_Victoria",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Docklands Stadium, originally Colonial Stadium, opened in March 2000 and now hosts major sports events.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Docklands%2C_Victoria",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "After containerisation, Docklands fell into disuse and became a hub for Melbourne’s underground rave scene in the 1990s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Docklands%2C_Victoria",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Victoria Harbour, part of Docklands, sits on traditional Kulin Nation lands of the Woiwurrung and Boonwurrung tribes.",
